    "mapping_notes": "# flashinfer__tinygemm2_sm100__deep_shallow_pdl_matrix__sm_100a\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in interface.json.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | bf16 | 8 x 1024 | input | logical activation A |\n| B | bf16 | 32 x 1024 | input | logical weight B; reference rows are output channels |\n| D | bf16 | 8 x 32 | output | D |\n| bias | bf16 | 32 | input | bias |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nThe reference uses A[m,k], B[n,k], and D[m,n]; B is stored with output-channel first.\nD[m,n] = sum_k A[m,k]*B[n,k].\nAdd bias[n] before storing the output.\nOptimized A element offset: m*K + k.\nOptimized B element offset: n*K + k.\nOptimized D element offset: m*N + n.\nReferences always store D at m*N+n; compare logical elements after this reindexing.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nCompiled to PTX and numerically checked on CPU. Not compared against an optimized\nGPU execution or proven equivalent. Precision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/b250399302acb2c4925b03416188c6678b762fbd/csrc/tinygemm2_sm100.cu\n"
